1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,870
Once tenants exist, you manage them from one list.

2
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:11,920
In this video, you edit, disable, enable, reload and remove tenants, and change several at once.

3
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:22,113
Tenants are managed from the Default tenant, by a user with the Manage tenants permission.

4
00:00:22,113 --> 00:00:24,379
Open Multi-Tenancy, then Tenants.

5
00:00:24,379 --> 00:00:28,332
Each row shows the name of a tenant, with badges for its state

6
00:00:28,332 --> 00:00:31,993
and, when they are set, its database provider and recipe.

7
00:00:32,444 --> 00:00:36,181
At the end of each row are the actions the tenant allows.

8
00:00:36,181 --> 00:00:41,164
A running tenant offers Edit, View, Disable and Reload, plus Features when the

9
00:00:41,164 --> 00:00:43,122
Features module is enabled.

10
00:00:43,122 --> 00:00:45,376
The Default tenant offers fewer:

11
00:00:45,376 --> 00:00:49,054
it has no Disable button, because it cannot be disabled.

12
00:00:49,515 --> 00:00:53,055
The search box finds tenants by name, host or prefix.

13
00:00:53,055 --> 00:00:57,075
Let's search for harbor, and the list narrows to that tenant.

14
00:00:57,538 --> 00:01:02,483
The State filter shows only running, disabled or uninitialized tenants.

15
00:01:02,483 --> 00:01:04,602
Let's choose Uninitialized:

16
00:01:04,602 --> 00:01:07,878
Pilot is the tenant that has not been set up.

17
00:01:12,078 --> 00:01:15,607
Every tenant has a state, shown as a badge in its row.

18
00:01:15,607 --> 00:01:18,371
Running means the tenant serves its site.

19
00:01:18,371 --> 00:01:22,018
Uninitialized means it exists, but nobody has set it up.

20
00:01:22,768 --> 00:01:27,243
Disabled means the tenant is switched off, with its settings and data kept.

21
00:01:27,243 --> 00:01:30,448
Initializing appears while a tenant is being set up.

22
00:01:31,198 --> 00:01:33,957
The actions of a row follow its state.

23
00:01:33,957 --> 00:01:39,161
Disable and View belong to running tenants, Enable to disabled ones, Setup to

24
00:01:39,161 --> 00:01:44,178
tenants that are not set up, and Remove to disabled or not set up tenants.

25
00:01:48,383 --> 00:01:51,549
To change a tenant, select Edit in its row.

26
00:01:51,549 --> 00:01:52,970
Let's edit Acme.

27
00:01:52,970 --> 00:01:58,203
The Edit Tenant page shows its name, which is read-only, then Category, Url

28
00:01:58,203 --> 00:02:00,723
Prefix, Description and Hostname.

29
00:02:01,174 --> 00:02:06,030
The Url Prefix and the Hostname decide which requests reach the tenant, so

30
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:07,730
change them with care.

31
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:10,704
Several domains can be separated by commas.

32
00:02:11,157 --> 00:02:14,899
Category and Description help you tell tenants apart.

33
00:02:14,899 --> 00:02:20,227
Let's type the category Customers, and the description Acme Bakery storefront.

34
00:02:20,683 --> 00:02:21,730
Select Save.

35
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:25,916
The tenant is reloaded with the settings you saved, and the row of

36
00:02:25,916 --> 00:02:28,823
Acme shows the category and the description.

37
00:02:29,297 --> 00:02:33,158
While a tenant is not set up, its Edit page also offers the

38
00:02:33,158 --> 00:02:36,188
recipe and database settings that Setup uses.

39
00:02:36,188 --> 00:02:37,376
Here is Pilot.

40
00:02:37,376 --> 00:02:40,287
A tenant that is set up does not show them.

41
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:47,940
To switch a tenant off, select Disable in its row.

42
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:49,583
Let's disable Harbor.

43
00:02:49,583 --> 00:02:51,713
A dialog asks you to confirm.

44
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:53,062
Select Ok.

45
00:02:53,062 --> 00:02:55,620
The state of Harbor changes to Disabled.

46
00:02:55,620 --> 00:03:00,402
The tenant stops serving its site, while its settings and data stay as they are.

47
00:03:00,861 --> 00:03:04,598
Its row offers Enable instead of View and Disable.

48
00:03:04,598 --> 00:03:10,138
Remove also appears, because this site allows removal, and only a disabled or

49
00:03:10,138 --> 00:03:12,741
not set up tenant can be removed.

50
00:03:13,199 --> 00:03:15,840
Select Enable to switch Harbor on again.

51
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,218
No dialog appears.

52
00:03:17,218 --> 00:03:21,409
The state returns to Running, and the tenant serves its site again.

53
00:03:25,648 --> 00:03:30,034
Reload makes one tenant start again, while the application keeps running.

54
00:03:30,034 --> 00:03:34,698
Its settings are read again, and the next request builds the tenant with them.

55
00:03:35,154 --> 00:03:36,769
Let's reload Harbor.

56
00:03:36,769 --> 00:03:38,695
Select Reload in its row.

57
00:03:38,695 --> 00:03:41,056
No dialog and no message appear:

58
00:03:41,056 --> 00:03:42,734
the list opens again.

59
00:03:43,225 --> 00:03:47,611
Use Reload after you change settings outside the admin screens.

60
00:03:47,611 --> 00:03:53,205
Saving the Edit Tenant page already reloads the tenant, so it needs no extra step.

61
00:03:57,426 --> 00:04:01,392
To change several tenants at once, tick their checkboxes.

62
00:04:01,392 --> 00:04:03,722
Let's select Juniper and Maple.

63
00:04:03,722 --> 00:04:09,326
With two or more selected, the toolbar shows how many, and an Actions menu appears.

64
00:04:09,793 --> 00:04:12,904
The Actions menu offers Disable and Enable.

65
00:04:12,904 --> 00:04:17,030
Choose Disable, and confirm the Bulk Action dialog with Ok.

66
00:04:17,030 --> 00:04:19,443
Both tenants change to Disabled.

67
00:04:19,931 --> 00:04:24,460
Disable applies to running tenants and Enable to disabled tenants.

68
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:30,751
Any other selected tenant is skipped with a warning, and the Default tenant is never disabled.

69
00:04:34,951 --> 00:04:37,254
Removing a tenant is off by default.

70
00:04:37,254 --> 00:04:42,246
Whoever runs the application allows it in the configuration, and the documentation of

71
00:04:42,246 --> 00:04:44,331
the Tenants module explains how.

72
00:04:45,081 --> 00:04:49,500
Even then, only a tenant that is disabled or not set up can be removed.

73
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:54,322
Removing it deletes its settings, its files and its database content for good.

74
00:04:54,322 --> 00:04:56,791
The Default tenant cannot be removed.

75
00:04:58,432 --> 00:05:01,831
Maple is disabled, so its row offers Remove.

76
00:05:01,831 --> 00:05:06,182
Select it, and a dialog titled Remove asks you to confirm.

77
00:05:06,634 --> 00:05:07,494
Select Ok.

78
00:05:07,494 --> 00:05:11,419
A message says that the tenant Maple was removed, and points to the

79
00:05:11,419 --> 00:05:13,355
log file for more information.

80
00:05:13,355 --> 00:05:15,774
The row of Maple is gone from the list.

81
00:05:17,774 --> 00:05:22,708
You can edit, disable, enable, reload and remove tenants from one list.

82
00:05:22,708 --> 00:05:24,374
Thanks for watching.

